<div class="legal">
<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>Ceppty is made by ZixyAero (KvK 97721379, the Netherlands). Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:support@ceppty.nl">support@ceppty.nl</a>.</p>
<h2>What data the app uses</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Receipts you add.</strong> The app reads the text from the PDF or photo (store, date, products, prices, discounts) and stores it in a database on your phone.</li>
<li><strong>Your settings</strong>, such as your own categories and the category you give a product.</li>
</ul>
<p>The app does not keep the PDF or photo for long: the copy of a PDF is deleted once it has been read; a photo stays on your phone until you confirm the receipt, at most 30 days. Your original file stays where it was.</p>
<h2>What we don't do</h2>
<ul>
<li>No account or sign-in.</li>
<li>Nothing about you is sent in the background. When you open the app, it checks our server in the EU for updated receipt-reading rules and category lists, at most twice a day: a plain file download that contains no data about you, your receipts or your phone, and we don't keep your IP address. Your data only leaves the phone when you tap “Send report”.</li>
<li>No analytics, no crash reporting, no ads, no tracking.</li>
<li>No selling or passing data to third parties.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Reports about a receipt</h2>
<p>If the app reads a receipt incorrectly, you can send us a report. Before sending you choose what it contains: the receipt text, technical details about how the app read it, and — only if you tick it and the receipt isn't confirmed yet — the photo itself. You can also write briefly what is wrong. A photo shows everything printed on the receipt. The app removes loyalty card and payment card numbers from the text before sending. You can add a name so we know who you are; there is no account. Each report also carries a random number the app creates once on your phone, so we can tell reports from the same phone apart and stop abuse. It is not your phone's advertising or device ID.</p>
<p>The report goes to our own server in the EU. We use it only to fix how the app reads receipts, keep it for at most 90 days and then delete it. To have your report deleted sooner, email us the report number the app shows after sending. We don't keep your IP address. If our server can't be reached, you try again later; the report is never sent by email or any other way. Our hosting provider and GitHub (where we track the fix, without the receipt text or file) process reports only on our behalf. We don't sell reports or share them with anyone else. After we fix a problem we may keep a short anonymised excerpt — products, prices, date and store branch, without names or card numbers — as test data, so the app keeps reading such receipts correctly.</p>
<h2>When you share something yourself</h2>
<p>You can also send files through your phone's share menu, for example an export of your spending. This only happens when you choose to, and you choose who receives it.</p>
<h2>Deleting your data</h2>
<p>You can delete receipts in the app. Uninstalling the app erases all of its data from your phone. We don't have a copy.</p>
<h2>Children</h2>
<p>The app is not meant for children and asks nobody for personal details.</p>
<h2>This website</h2>
<p>ceppty.nl uses no cookies and no analytics, and loads nothing from other websites — even the fonts are on our own server. We don't keep your IP address.</p>
<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If anything in this policy changes, we'll update this page and the date above.</p>
